# Tapered ink on closed curves, 192x96. Every stroke is dark ink on a closed curve, and no stroke has a round cap.
# Left: a square through its 4 corners, tension:0, starting at the top left, with stroke:p.ink,[2 14 2 14]. The top
# left and bottom right corners are thin (2px). The top right and bottom left corners are thick (14px). Each side
# swells or thins steadily between its corners, the closing left side included. The top left corner has no blob.
# Middle: a smooth loop through 4 points with taper:.3, starting at the left point. The stroke thins to a point at the
# left on both sides of the seam and is full width at the right.
# Right: a triangle through 3 corners, tension:0, starting at the top, with stroke:p.ink,[2 8 14]. The top corner is
# thinnest, the bottom right is medium, and the bottom left is thickest. The closing side runs from 14px back to 2px.
@target shapes/closed_ink.png 192x96

curve -20,-20 20,-20 20,20 -20,20 closed tension:0 stroke:p.ink,[2 14 2 14] at:32,48
curve -22,0 0,-22 22,0 0,22 closed stroke:p.ink,6 taper:.3 at:96,48
curve 0,-22 22,18 -22,18 closed tension:0 stroke:p.ink,[2 8 14] at:160,48
